## Version Numbering

Follow [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/):

- **MAJOR** (X.0.0) - Incompatible API changes, breaking changes
- **MINOR** (0.X.0) - Backward-compatible new functionality
- **PATCH** (0.0.X) - Backward-compatible bug fixes

### Examples
- `v1.00.00.md` → v1.0.0 (Initial release)
- `v1.01.00.md` → v1.1.0 (New feature, backward compatible)
- `v1.01.01.md` → v1.1.1 (Bug fix)
- `v2.00.00.md` → v2.0.0 (Breaking changes)

---

## Writing Guidelines

### Be Specific
❌ BAD: "Improved performance"
✅ GOOD: "Reduced MAX_QUERY_RECORDS from 200 to 100 for 30% faster queries"

### Use Active Voice
❌ BAD: "The email template was updated"
✅ GOOD: "Updated email template to show job context"

### Include Context
❌ BAD: "Added JobContext class"
✅ GOOD: "Added JobContext class to encapsulate job metadata (SOLID Single Responsibility Principle)"

### Provide Examples
Always include code examples for:
- New features
- Changed APIs
- Migration steps
- Configuration changes

### Link to Relevant Code
When referencing specific changes, include file paths:
```markdown
- Enhanced `AgentErrorMonitorService.cls` with JobContext
- Updated `AgentErrorMonitorBatch.cls` to pass job metadata
```

